{"event_type":"review","id":"db4afe68ce61f310f9d30f057ea46c505cce9c8c12e8388ddf6fe323fcd4908d","occurred_at":"2026-11-06T10:27:42Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ce2ab2419ede89c540859bff90fc626288b86d83da6f7d712f2e1bfc9c4b4592","sha256":"ce2ab2419ede89c540859bff90fc626288b86d83da6f7d712f2e1bfc9c4b4592"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/048494e2cadf9a8a29f27aac6f2af80457f2c1c620029044290880de661ebd29","sha256":"048494e2cadf9a8a29f27aac6f2af80457f2c1c620029044290880de661ebd29"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a4075d8508946ed875215099bee5ee2e6f3e48125acb2dd9792e48b7594972a1","sha256":"a4075d8508946ed875215099bee5ee2e6f3e48125acb2dd9792e48b7594972a1"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/bb66bd455c9258a100ccc36102a860eb565c0da84860aca7203b5fe24fd9ed1f","sha256":"bb66bd455c9258a100ccc36102a860eb565c0da84860aca7203b5fe24fd9ed1f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0669930d921412b1d4ed632315366e6a14809b493654d133c9683fc88c828eb6","sha256":"0669930d921412b1d4ed632315366e6a14809b493654d133c9683fc88c828eb6"}],"attempt_id":"e703a7c3362738fe21052b9c13b44edb9e59eb2b498849aec1a665bd8334237b:0:1","base":"8e104a9a98d213fb55ade10cb8d241b916da8f68","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"0cdf422e843c9f99d1db5a79694291aaec8c7aca","body":"**Only treat `---`/`+++` as file headers before the first `@@` hunk.**\n\n`secret_scan_diff` (apps/crq-python/crq.py:422-426) treats every line that starts with `+++ ` or `--- ` as a file header. Inside a hunk, an added line with content `++ X` appears as `+++ X`. A removed line with content `-- X` appears as `--- X`. Removed SQL or Lua comment lines (`-- ...`) are a common example.\n\nWhen the scan reads such a content line as a header:\n- The scan never checks that line against the denylist rules.\n- `path` becomes the line's content. Later lines in the same file are matched against the wrong path. Path-scoped rules (`prx`) can then skip them, and the `ALLOWLIST_PATHS` check can wrongly exclude them.\n\nThis check is the only gate before the diff is uploaded to the vendor. An added line such as `++ <token>` therefore passes the denylist. Gitleaks is a second check, but it runs only when it is installed (apps/crq-python/crq.py:444).\n\nTrack the header state from `diff --git`, and end it at the first `@@`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔒️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     path = None\n+    in_header = False\n     for n, line in enumerate(diff.splitlines(), 1):\n-        if line.startswith(\"+++ \") or line.startswith(\"--- \"):\n-            p = line[4:]\n-            if p != \"/dev/null\":\n-                path = p[2:] if p[:2] in (\"a/\", \"b/\") else p\n-            continue\n         if line.startswith(\"diff --git\"):\n             m = re.match(r\"diff --git a/(.*) b/(.*)$\", line)\n             path = m.group(2) if m else None\n+            in_header = True\n+            continue\n+        if line.startswith(\"@@\"):\n+            in_header = False\n+            continue\n+        if in_header:\n+            if line.startswith(\"+++ \") or line.startswith(\"--- \"):\n+                p = line[4:]\n+                if p != \"/dev/null\":\n+                    path = p[2:] if p[:2] in (\"a/\", \"b/\") else p\n             continue\n         if not line or line[0] not in \"+-\" or path is None:\n             continue\n```\n</details>","id":"262bfb59ea870c82a236b27f00230b0938259432b2702f7d72750b36971d60a2","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Only treat `---`/`+++` as file headers before the first `@@` hunk."}],"head":"331c946973892acf20c538bef181ddc3856ca718","head_tree":"a619b07177492e5c80d4ce45880731ec409f8b2c","input_scope":[{"blob":"0cdf422e843c9f99d1db5a79694291aaec8c7aca","intervals":[[1,3585]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq.py"}],"job_id":"e703a7c3362738fe21052b9c13b44edb9e59eb2b498849aec1a665bd8334237b:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"0cdf422e843c9f99d1db5a79694291aaec8c7aca","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/crq.py","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"0cdf422e843c9f99d1db5a79694291aaec8c7aca","intervals":[[34,34],[37,39],[84,92],[128,129],[299,307],[313,319],[322,323],[325,326],[328,328],[333,333],[335,335],[338,338],[340,340],[348,355],[366,373],[396,402],[406,407],[409,410],[413,414],[416,416],[622,623],[760,765],[777,777],[802,803],[909,909],[916,916],[954,961],[964,965],[968,968],[987,988],[998,999],[1015,1015],[1027,1027],[1032,1032],[1050,1050],[1054,1054],[1056,1057],[1060,1062],[1713,1718],[1740,1740],[1743,1743],[1745,1745],[1754,1756],[1758,1762],[1785,1786],[1842,1862],[1864,1866],[1868,1869],[1881,1881],[1888,1888],[1890,1902],[1904,1904],[1910,1910],[1921,1923],[1955,1955],[2189,2238],[2299,2354],[2376,2381],[2404,2415],[2527,2532],[2535,2537],[2561,2562],[2613,2614],[2790,2794],[2798,2798],[2905,2915],[3028,3030],[3037,3037],[3048,3061],[3076,3078],[3101,3115],[3121,3121],[3142,3143],[3168,3170],[3178,3178],[3180,3181],[3435,3440],[3486,3496]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq.py"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"0cdf422e843c9f99d1db5a79694291aaec8c7aca","intervals":[[34,34],[37,39],[84,92],[128,129],[299,307],[313,319],[322,323],[325,326],[328,328],[333,333],[335,335],[338,338],[340,340],[348,355],[366,373],[396,402],[406,407],[409,410],[413,414],[416,416],[622,623],[760,765],[777,777],[802,803],[909,909],[916,916],[954,961],[964,965],[968,968],[987,988],[998,999],[1015,1015],[1027,1027],[1032,1032],[1050,